adr: 0360
file: lib/dialect/pastoml.pas
kills: lib_toml_errors
why: Descend stops refusing a header that passes through a table a dotted key created, so `a.b = 1` followed by `[a]` is accepted. That is TOML's one-definition rule read the lenient way, and it is the half of the format a parser is likeliest to get wrong: the rules turn on how a table came to exist and not on whether it exists. Two lines of the golden turn into ACCEPTED (should not be).
--- old
      else if forHeader and got^.dotted then begin
        e := errSyntax;
        cur := nil
      end
--- new
      else if forHeader and got^.dotted then
        cur := got
